# Make UPower see the ASUS charge-limit attribute (ARCHITECTURE §6.4).
#
# The ACPI battery driver registers BAT0 at boot. asus-nb-wmi loads seconds later and
# adds charge_control_end_threshold to BAT0 with device_create_file(), which sends no
# uevent. UPower's 60-upower-battery.rules imports CHARGE_LIMIT from its hwdb only when
# that attribute exists while a BAT0 event is processed, so without a new event UPower
# reports ChargeThresholdSupported=false and the battery charges to 100 %.
#
# asus-wmi registers its battery hook during probe, so the attribute exists by the
# time the driver's "bind" event arrives. This rule then asks the kernel for a "change"
# event on BAT0, and 60-upower-battery.rules runs again with the attribute present.
# `udevadm trigger` only writes to BAT0's uevent file and returns; it waits for
# nothing, so it is safe as a short RUN program. It cannot trigger itself: the new
# event is for power_supply, not platform.
# upower.service waits for the result (upower.service.d/10-apex-wait-threshold.conf).

ACTION=="bind", SUBSYSTEM=="platform", DRIVER=="asus-nb-wmi", \
  TEST=="/sys/class/power_supply/BAT0", \
  RUN+="/usr/bin/udevadm trigger --action=change /sys/class/power_supply/BAT0"
